\\sqrt{2}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355007 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355007 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355007 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "290f4389-144e-58ae-8aa0-f8779961574c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355251 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355251 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355251 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "426fd857-13b1-5ab3-9758-9722e35fc330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355266 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355266 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355266 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "435fb70d-dab8-537c-a107-ef7870828b02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356025 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "994c1016-eda3-584d-9ca2-ccfb245592f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356741 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356741 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356741 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee2df7b5-bcfb-56b5-bfec-d5975826e4f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357204 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357204 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357204 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186